IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-companies-domain`

§ `Part 4 — Shares, Debentures and Charges`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), Part 4, ss 43–141.
-- Source: SSO current version as at 07 Sep 2026.
--
-- Division 1 (ss 43–58) is entirely repealed.
-- This encoding covers the computable rules in Divisions 2–8.
-- ===========================================================================


§§ `Division 2 — Restrictions on allotment`


§§§ `s 59 — Allotment of shares in public company`

-- s 59(1): public company not issuing prospectus must give 3-day notice
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 59(1)"
`pre allotment notice days` MEANS 3


§§ `Division 3 — Shares`


§§§ `s 62A — No par value shares`

-- s 62A(1): all shares have no par value (declaratory, post-2006)
-- s 62A(3): amounts received = paid-up share capital


§§§ `s 63A — Return on allotment`

-- s 63A(1): within 14 days of allotment, lodge return with Registrar
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 63A(1)"
`allotment return lodgement days` MEANS 14


§§§ `s 64 — Power of company to alter share capital`

-- s 64(1): company may by ordinary resolution alter share capital
-- (procedural — the power exists, conditions are in constitution)


§§§ `s 74 — Class rights variation`

-- s 74(1): variation requires specified proportion or 75% of class
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 74(1)"
`default class rights variation threshold pct` MEANS 75

-- s 74(1AA): holders of >= 5% of class may apply to Court
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 74(1AA)"
GIVEN `percentage of class shares held` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has standing to oppose class rights variation` IF
    `percentage of class shares held` AT LEAST 5

-- s 74(1AA): application deadline — 1 month
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 74(1AA)"
`class rights variation opposition period months` MEANS 1


§§§ `s 76 — Financial assistance for share acquisition`

-- s 76(9A): board-only whitelist — assistance permitted if <= 10%
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 76(9A)"
GIVEN `outstanding assistance amount`  IS A NUMBER
    , `paid up capital`                IS A NUMBER
    , `reserves`                       IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `financial assistance within board only limit` IF
    `outstanding assistance amount` AT MOST
        ((`paid up capital` PLUS `reserves`) TIMES 0.1)

-- s 76(9A)(d): member notice deadline — 10 business days
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 76(9A)(d)"
`financial assistance member notice business days` MEANS 10

-- s 76(9B): assistance must be given within 12 months of resolution
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 76(9B)"
`financial assistance resolution validity months` MEANS 12


§§§ `s 76B — Share buyback volume cap`

-- s 76B(3): 20% cap on ordinary share buybacks during relevant period
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 76B(3)"
GIVEN `shares purchased in period`      IS A NUMBER
    , `total shares at resolution date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `share buyback within volume cap` IF
    `shares purchased in period` AT MOST
        (`total shares at resolution date` TIMES 0.2)

-- s 76B(3B): same 20% cap for non-redeemable preference shares
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 76B(3B)"
GIVEN `pref shares purchased`          IS A NUMBER
    , `total pref shares at resolution` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `pref share buyback within volume cap` IF
    `pref shares purchased` AT MOST
        (`total pref shares at resolution` TIMES 0.2)


§§§ `s 76D — Selective off-market buyback`

-- s 76D(2A): consent of 75% of affected class required
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 76D(2A)"
`selective buyback class consent threshold pct` MEANS 75


§§§ `s 76F — Solvency test for buyback payments`

-- s 76F(4): three-limb solvency test
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 76F(4)"
GIVEN `no ground for inability to pay debts`     IS A BOOLEAN
    , `intending to wind up within 12 months`    IS A BOOLEAN
    , `can pay debts in full within 12 months of winding up` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `can pay debts as they fall due in next 12 months`     IS A BOOLEAN
    , `assets not less than liabilities before`   IS A BOOLEAN
    , `assets not less than liabilities after`    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `company is solvent for buyback` IF
        `no ground for inability to pay debts`
    AND (IF `intending to wind up within 12 months`
         THEN `can pay debts in full within 12 months of winding up`
         ELSE `can pay debts as they fall due in next 12 months`)
    AND `assets not less than liabilities before`
    AND `assets not less than liabilities after`

-- s 76F(3): penalty for approving buyback while insolvent
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 76F(3)"
`penalty for insolvent buyback approval` MEANS 100000
`imprisonment for insolvent buyback years` MEANS 3


§§§ `s 76I — Treasury share cap`

-- s 76I(1),(2): treasury shares must not exceed 10% of class
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 76I(1)–(2)"
GIVEN `treasury shares in class` IS A NUMBER
    , `total shares in class`   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `treasury share limit exceeded` IF
    `treasury shares in class` GREATER THAN
        (`total shares in class` TIMES 0.1)

-- s 76I(3): disposal period for excess treasury shares
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 76I(3)"
`excess treasury share disposal months` MEANS 6


§§§ `s 76K — Treasury share sale: cash definition`

-- s 76K(2)(d): "cash" includes undertaking to pay within 90 days
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 76K(2)(d)"
`treasury share sale payment deadline days` MEANS 90


§§§ `s 77 — Options over unissued shares`

-- s 77(1): public company general option — void after 5 years
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 77(1)"
`general option maximum years` MEANS 5

-- s 77(1A): employee/director option — void after 10 years
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 77(1A)"
`employee option maximum years` MEANS 10


§§§ `s 78 — Interest charged to capital`

-- s 78: rate cap and period cap
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 78"
`maximum interest rate on capital pct` MEANS 5
`maximum interest period after completion months` MEANS 12


§§ `Division 3A — Reduction of share capital`


§§§ `s 78B — Private company capital reduction`

-- s 78B(1): private company may reduce capital by special resolution if solvent
-- s 78B(2): solvency requirement waived if no cash/asset distribution
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 78B(2)"
GIVEN `involves cash or asset distribution` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `involves release of liability`      IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `solvency requirement applies to reduction` IF
    `involves cash or asset distribution`
    OR `involves release of liability`

-- s 78B(3): solvency statement timing for private company
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 78B(3)"
`private company solvency statement max days before resolution` MEANS 20


§§§ `s 78C — Public company capital reduction`

-- s 78C(3): solvency statement timing for public company
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 78C(3)"
`public company solvency statement max days before resolution` MEANS 30

-- s 78C(3)(b): lodge with Registrar within 15 days of resolution
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 78C(3)(b)"
`public company solvency statement lodgement days` MEANS 15


§§§ `s 78D — Creditor objection`

-- s 78D(2): creditor objection window — 6 weeks
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 78D(2)"
`creditor objection period weeks` MEANS 6


§§§ `s 78E — Effective date of reduction`

-- s 78E(1)(a),(b): lodgement windows
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 78E(1)"
`reduction lodgement window start weeks` MEANS 6
`reduction lodgement window end weeks` MEANS 8

-- s 78E(1)(c): if creditor objections — 15 days from dismissal
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 78E(1)(c)"
`reduction lodgement after objection dismissal days` MEANS 15


§§§ `s 78I — Court-approved reduction`

-- s 78I(3): lodge within 90 days of court order
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 78I(3)"
`court approved reduction lodgement days` MEANS 90


§§§ `s 78K — Liability cap post-reduction`

-- s 78K: member liability after reduction
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 78K"
GIVEN `issue price`     IS A NUMBER
    , `amount paid up`  IS A NUMBER
    , `amount reduced`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `residual call liability` IS
    `issue price` MINUS (`amount paid up` PLUS `amount reduced`)


§§ `Division 4 — Substantial shareholdings`


§§§ `s 81 — Substantial shareholding threshold`

-- s 81(1): substantial shareholder = >= 5% of total votes
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 81(1)"
GIVEN `votes attached to shares held` IS A NUMBER
    , `total votes in company`       IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is substantial shareholder` IF
    `votes attached to shares held` AT LEAST
        (`total votes in company` TIMES 0.05)

-- s 81(2): same test per class for multi-class companies
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 81(2)"
GIVEN `votes in class held`   IS A NUMBER
    , `total votes in class`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is substantial shareholder in class` IF
    `votes in class held` AT LEAST
        (`total votes in class` TIMES 0.05)


§§§ `s 82 — Notification of substantial shareholding`

-- s 82(2)(b): notice within 2 business days
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 82(2)(b)"
`substantial shareholder initial notice business days` MEANS 2


§§§ `s 83 — Change in percentage level`

-- s 83(1): notice within 2 business days of change
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 83(1)"
`substantial shareholder change notice business days` MEANS 2


§§§ `s 84 — Cessation of substantial shareholding`

-- s 84(2): notice within 2 business days
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 84(2)"
`substantial shareholder cessation notice business days` MEANS 2


§§ `Division 5 — Debentures`


§§§ `s 100 — Irredeemable debenture enforcement`

-- s 100(1)(b): enforcement threshold — 60% of outstanding principal
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 100(1)(b)"
GIVEN `realisation value`       IS A NUMBER
    , `outstanding principal`   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `debenture security enforceable` IF
    `realisation value` AT MOST
        (`outstanding principal` TIMES 0.6)


§§ `Division 7 — Title and transfers`


§§§ `s 125 — Duplicate share certificate`

-- s 125(2): surety bond required if shares/debentures > $500
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 125(2)"
`duplicate certificate surety threshold` MEANS 500


§§§ `s 130AE — Share certificate timing`

-- s 130AE: deadlines for issuing share certificates
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 130AE"
`share certificate after allotment days` MEANS 60
`share certificate after transfer days` MEANS 30


§§ `Division 8 — Registration of charges`


§§§ `s 131 — Charge registration deadline`

-- s 131(1): 30-day deadline — charge void against liquidator/creditors if missed
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 131(1)"
`charge registration deadline days` MEANS 30


-- ===========================================================================
-- TEST CASES
-- ===========================================================================

§§ `Part 4 — Illustrations`

-- s 74: class rights variation standing
#ASSERT `has standing to oppose class rights variation` 5
#ASSERT `has standing to oppose class rights variation` 15
#ASSERT NOT (`has standing to oppose class rights variation` 4)

-- s 76(9A): financial assistance board-only limit
-- 10% of (capital + reserves) = 10% of (1000000 + 500000) = 150000
#ASSERT `financial assistance within board only limit` 150000 1000000 500000
#ASSERT `financial assistance within board only limit` 100000 1000000 500000
#ASSERT NOT (`financial assistance within board only limit` 200000 1000000 500000)

-- s 76B(3): share buyback volume cap (20%)
-- 20% of 1000000 = 200000
#ASSERT `share buyback within volume cap` 200000 1000000
#ASSERT NOT (`share buyback within volume cap` 250000 1000000)

-- s 76F(4): solvency test
-- Solvent: no grounds, not winding up, can pay as due, assets >= liabilities
#ASSERT `company is solvent for buyback` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Insolvent: grounds exist
#ASSERT NOT (`company is solvent for buyback` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- Insolvent: winding up but cannot pay in full
#ASSERT NOT (`company is solvent for buyback` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- Solvent: winding up and can pay in full
#ASSERT `company is solvent for buyback` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE

-- s 76I: treasury share cap (10%)
-- 1100 treasury shares of 10000 total = 11% -> exceeded
#ASSERT `treasury share limit exceeded` 1100 10000
-- 900 of 10000 = 9% -> not exceeded
#ASSERT NOT (`treasury share limit exceeded` 900 10000)

-- s 78B(2): solvency requirement for capital reduction
#ASSERT `solvency requirement applies to reduction` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `solvency requirement applies to reduction` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`solvency requirement applies to reduction` FALSE FALSE)

-- s 78K: residual call liability
-- issue price 10, paid up 6, reduced 2 = liability 2
`test residual liability` MEANS `residual call liability` 10 6 2
#ASSERT `test residual liability` EQUALS 2

-- s 81: substantial shareholding (5% threshold)
-- 50000 votes of 1000000 = 5% -> substantial
#ASSERT `is substantial shareholder` 50000 1000000
-- 40000 of 1000000 = 4% -> not substantial
#ASSERT NOT (`is substantial shareholder` 40000 1000000)

-- s 100: debenture enforcement (60% threshold)
-- realisation 500000, principal 1000000 -> 50% <= 60% -> enforceable
#ASSERT `debenture security enforceable` 500000 1000000
-- realisation 700000, principal 1000000 -> 70% > 60% -> not enforceable
#ASSERT NOT (`debenture security enforceable` 700000 1000000)
